.TH MOXY-CHECK-MOXINS 1 "" "moxy"
.SH NAME
moxy-check-moxins \- Check that a directory of moxins loads, listing every failure
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B moxy check-moxins
.RI --dir = STRING
.SH DESCRIPTION
Loads the moxin at --dir, or every moxin in its subdirectories, with the loader the server uses, and prints every tool file that fails with the reason. Exits 1 if any moxin fails, 0 otherwise; it reads files only and starts nothing. This is the intended per-repo gate for shipped moxin directories: a repo that ships moxins runs it on them (a justfile recipe or a flake check), so a file the loader would refuse fails that repo's merge gate, not every session that later loads the moxin.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --dir (required)
A moxin directory (holds _moxin.toml) or a directory whose subdirectories are moxins.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR moxy (1)
